{"content":[{"c":["HOBAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town to which Abraham pursued the armies under Chedorlaomer (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.15","r":"Gen.14.15","rawR":"Gen.14.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.15","value":"Gen.14.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:15"},"). Its location is uncertain, but various suggestions have been made. Some equate it with the Hobah about 50 miles (80 kilometers) northwest of Damascus; others, with the territory called Ube in the Amarna letters; and still others, with Tell el-Salihite, 10 miles (16 kilometers) east of Damascus."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hobah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 14:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.15","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.15","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d508dabfa60f9762929f1c78da79944bfaf1fcfb12f427883203fe5a53bb8531","sourceItemName":"Hobah","sourceItemOrder":313,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hobah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hobah","title":"Hobah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}